=== CORRECTION 2026-08-25 (review round 2) — appended, log body NOT rewritten
Two statements in the section-3 body above are wrong and are withdrawn here.

(1) Lines 57-59 say option (b) "lands in the SEQ MOV/EMB address path, which
    is one of the three classes that carried waived endpoints on build_034
    (evidence/qwen2b/rb/TIMING.md: seq_0 MOV addressing, 3 endpoints)".
    The waived class is sequencer **MOV addressing ONLY** — all three of its
    endpoints are MOV-path (shipped_roll_endpoint_census.log:133,:154,:156) —
    and docs/QWEN2B_QUANT_STUDY.md:226-227 records that the R6 **EMB** 5-bit
    barrel shift does NOT appear in either of the two worst violating paths.
    Correct statement: option (b) is new logic ADJACENT to a waived class, in
    a block that closes at WNS 0.000 with zero margin — not logic inside a
    waived class.

(2) Line 63 says EMBLOG2 is "a 4-bit log2".  It is FIVE bits:
    rtl/seq_unit.sv:298 `logic [4:0] emb_row_log2;`, with EMBLOG2_MIN/MAX =
    5'd8 / 5'd13 at :289.  The [8,13] range the log prints is right; the
    width is not.

Neither correction moves the section's arithmetic: the option-B matvec penalty
(x1.0008), the 4B padding cost (+727.5 MiB) and the EMBLOG2-13 ceiling finding
are all unaffected.
